ab377df-73df-53f2-81bc-0c28114d3720" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446323} {:answer/id #uuid "6358e671-90b3-5914-a718-8213a1f17a31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446325} {:answer/id #uuid "65a82f6c-7a03-5152-b67b-6b75c8f2f8df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446326} {:answer/id #uuid "720f0040-8787-5886-9c1c-402554299b56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446330} {:answer/id #uuid "f701af70-1e73-5b6a-b0c6-4b6e59b2fa9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446358}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6358e671-90b3-5914-a718-8213a1f17a31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446325} :answer-field/id #uuid "dd81b3b5-e497-5c05-9bc7-9bf55e4547fa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446369}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "833e6fc8-0df5-5faa-ab1e-b5f4126e71c3" :question/math-academy-id "q-141215" :question/problem "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $6\\times 6$ matrix and $A$ is invertible,  then $\\underline{\\phantom{xxxxxx}}$ .*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\nI. $det(A)=0$\n\nII. $\\text{Null}(A)={R}^{6}$\n\nIII. $\\text{dim(Col}(A))=6$" :question/worked-solution "If $A$ is an $6\\times 6$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $$\n\\displaystyle \\,⇔\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\text{Col}(A) &={R}^{6} \\\\ \\text{dim(Col}(A)) &=6=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\ \\text{Null}(A) &=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\text{dim(Null}(A)) &=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $6\\times 6$ matrix and $A$ is invertible,  then $det(A)=0$* $\\,\\times$ \n\nSince the matrix $A$ is invertible, it must be  $det(A)\\ne 0.$\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $6\\times 6$ matrix and $A$ is invertible,  then  $\\text{Null}(A)={R}^{6}.$* $\\,\\times$\n\nIndeed, since $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem,  we have $\\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\}.$\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $6\\times 6$ matrix and $A$ is invertible,  then $\\text{dim(Col}(A))=6.$* $\\,✓$ \n\nSince $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{dim(Col}(A))=6.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446378 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5fb3aa43-1e84-516c-8972-6a71a1a76857" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446324} {:answer/id #uuid "bd0f6e35-d7c3-5c27-95f6-6b6b01493577" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446343} {:answer/id #uuid "d9adf053-ad3b-5a09-87f7-674bd680f4dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446348} {:answer/id #uuid "db451e16-e9ec-50a7-a360-3e56d95fe251" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446350} {:answer/id #uuid "f36d2201-ba87-5be6-b825-8ab2db34fb07" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446354}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5fb3aa43-1e84-516c-8972-6a71a1a76857" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446324} :answer-field/id #uuid "1fa1830b-5add-5daf-9fd3-0b3e06eb4a22" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446362}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "a9326523-4bce-5554-9699-fb91223b9531" :question/math-academy-id "q-142479" :question/problem "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{rank}(A)<n,$ then $\\underline{\\phantom{xxxxxx}}\\,.$*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\nI. $A$ is invertible\n\nII. $\\text{Null}(A)$ has no basis\n\nIII. $det(A)=0$" :question/worked-solution "The invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $$\n\\displaystyle \\,⇔\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\text{Col}(A) &={R}^{n} \\\\ \\text{dim(Col}(A)) &=n=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\ \\text{Null}(A) &=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\text{dim(Null}(A)) &=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{rank}(A)<n,$ then  $A$ is invertible.* $\\,\\times$ \n\nSince $\\text{rank}(A)<n,$  then according to the invertible matrix theorem, $A$ can't be invertible.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{rank}(A)<n,$ then  $\\text{Null}(A)$ has no basis.* $\\,\\times$\n\nIndeed, since $A$ is *not* invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0,$ which means that $\\text{Null}(A)$ actually has a basis.\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{rank}(A)<n,$ then  $det(A)=0.$* $\\,✓$  \n\nIndeed, since $A$ is not invertible it must be $det(A)=0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446379 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3307d8dd-316e-59b9-a236-3cf5704a1eda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{dim(Null}(A))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446318} {:answer/id #uuid "5962da19-877d-530f-b40f-aae8873a783f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{nullity}(A)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446322} {:answer/id #uuid "9a43c232-d1ff-5d5b-967a-f97c5c62802c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{rank}(A)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446337} {:answer/id #uuid "abf5dd86-5e61-586c-8e5b-345ea680eb42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{Col}(A)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446342} {:answer/id #uuid "ee0fb303-98ae-5122-984e-1ef2c8e57d8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{Null}(A)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446352}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9a43c232-d1ff-5d5b-967a-f97c5c62802c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{rank}(A)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446337} :answer-field/id #uuid "9e061b51-851a-5ec1-9247-2cb4ee8e99e6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446367}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e7063fa7-cfd5-5cea-b242-ca27bb233616" :question/math-academy-id "q-141194" :question/problem "$$\nA\\text{ is invertible}\\,⇔\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\text{Col}(A) &={R}^{n} \\\\ \\text{dim(Col}(A)) &=n=\\bbox[3pt,white,border: 2px solid Gainsboro]{\\phantom{W}} \\\\ \\text{Null}(A) &=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\text{dim(Null}(A)) &=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nConsider the equivalence above, where $A$ is an $n\\,\\times \\,n$ matrix. Which of the following should be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the *invertible matrix theorem* states the following: \n\n*Let $A$ be an $n\\,\\times \\,n$ matrix. Then we have the following equivalence:*\n\n$$\nA\\text{ is invertible}\\,⇔\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\text{Col}(A) &={R}^{n} \\\\ \\text{dim(Col}(A)) &=n=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\ \\text{Null}(A) &=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\text{dim(Null}(A)) &=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expression is $\\text{rank}(A).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446380 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d49a551-9ec5-52ad-a34a-89d55b7486b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446313} {:answer/id #uuid "2487a691-60de-5d0e-a46b-689f90f253ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446315} {:answer/id #uuid "41750c54-9a68-5140-acec-016759823bad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446319} {:answer/id #uuid "662ea6db-c29f-5f39-b454-f93e28a4789e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446327} {:answer/id #uuid "a1868d1e-0ee5-5742-b6e3-4792cb79e39e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446340}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a1868d1e-0ee5-5742-b6e3-4792cb79e39e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446340} :answer-field/id #uuid "fb932edd-7a39-5566-85fa-5d17f1b76d5d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446370}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "ec73c900-b909-5aa7-beeb-5f5b6ee2fba4" :question/math-academy-id "q-141341" :question/problem "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then  $\\underline{\\phantom{xxxxxx}}\\,.$*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\nI. $A$ is invertible\n\nII. $det(A)=0$\n\nIII. $\\text{dim(Col}(A))=n$" :question/worked-solution "The invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $$\n\\displaystyle \\,⇔\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\text{Col}(A) &={R}^{n} \\\\ \\text{dim(Col}(A)) &=n=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\ \\text{Null}(A) &=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\text{dim(Null}(A)) &=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then $A$ is invertible.* $\\,✓$\n\nIndeed, by the invertible matrix theorem, since $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ we must have that $A$ is invertible.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then $det(A)=0.$* $\\,\\times$ \n\nSince $A$ is invertible, then we must have $det(A)\\ne 0.$\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then $\\text{dim(Col}(A))=n.$*  $\\,✓$\n\nIndeed, since $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{dim(Col}(A))=n.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529139 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6c0bd5dd-c5f7-5e5d-b21c-bcdb4e2b830b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528560} {:answer/id #uuid "7385e402-bf26-5641-9a0b-660e87ee9d07" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528567} {:answer/id #uuid "e0746457-062b-51a1-b39b-1801dcc9dd24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528849} {:answer/id #uuid "e15f2509-6136-5ef5-b754-59b129df8ee9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528852} {:answer/id #uuid "f4fb30e2-e856-5197-b6a2-1b2e5bd62f64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528903}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e0746457-062b-51a1-b39b-1801dcc9dd24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528849} :answer-field/id #uuid "255a02e5-2e2c-5989-905e-69f5223274a6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528960}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "74f4be02-4fe9-5741-a4d1-7268f77a2f5f" :question/math-academy-id "q-142472" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and  $det(A)=-1?$ \n\nI. $A$ is **not** invertible\n\nII. $\\text{rank}(A)=3$\n\nIII. $A$ has $4$ pivot columns" :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $$\n\\displaystyle \\,⇔\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\text{Col}(A) &={R}^{3} \\\\ \\text{dim(Col}(A)) &=3=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\ \\text{Null}(A) &=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\text{dim(Null}(A)) &=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn. \n\n- Statement I is false. Indeed,   a matrix $A$ is invertible if and only if $det(A)\\ne 0.$ Since here we have $det(A)=-1\\ne 0,$ our matrix $A$ must be invertible.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, by the invertible matrix theorem\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\text{rank}(A)=3.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $\\text{rank}(A)=3$,  it must be $\\text{dim(Col}(A))=3$ which, in turn, means that  $A$ has $3$ pivot columns, not $4.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529191 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5d885553-3afc-5696-a382-4c860965f60c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528520} {:answer/id #uuid "7bf00a72-f79f-582d-9aaa-38874ff20b92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528592} {:answer/id #uuid "7df12baa-7b1b-58dc-8f63-3871724e61dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528598} {:answer/id #uuid "c974d506-c2bc-5e7b-97a4-c51ae5371031" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528794} {:answer/id #uuid "e94c076f-c6c7-517d-8c55-d74158a4a6fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528875}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5d885553-3afc-5696-a382-4c860965f60c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528520} :answer-field/id #uuid "20580d7d-28aa-5c7c-a048-784d0bfa2d4b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528956}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "f1d7f6a4-6114-5671-a52c-7df48bee5e24" :question/math-academy-id "q-141342" :question/problem "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)\\ne 0,$ then  $\\underline{\\phantom{xxxxxx}}\\,.$*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\nI. $\\text{Null}(A)$ has no basis\n\nII. $A$ is **not** invertible\n\nIII. All columns of $A$ are pivot columns" :question/worked-solution "The invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $$\n\\displaystyle \\,⇔\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\text{Col}(A) &={R}^{n} \\\\ \\text{dim(Col}(A)) &=n=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\ \\text{Null}(A) &=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\text{dim(Null}(A)) &=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately. \n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then $\\text{Null}(A)$ has no basis.* $\\,\\times$ \n\nSince $\\text{nullity}(A)\\ne 0,$ we have $\\text{Null}(A)\\ne \\{0\\}$ which, in turn, means that $\\text{Null}(A)$ must have a basis.\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then $A$ is **not** invertible.* $\\,✓$\n\nIndeed, by the invertible matrix theorem, since $\\text{nullity}(A)\\ne 0,$ we must have that $A$ is **not** invertible.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then all columns of $A$ are pivot columns.* $\\,\\times$\n\nSince $A$ is not invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{Col}(A)\\ne {R}^{n},$ which means that not all columns of $A$ are pivot columns.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186616956 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11608109-63f4-5381-863e-6e92792cc660" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616410} {:answer/id #uuid "70ead1a7-c4f0-5c8f-b43c-6dc1d4b49e9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616574} {:answer/id #uuid "8d64e571-5d10-561a-ab42-498565eee28f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616623} {:answer/id #uuid "c9871779-87ac-5527-9f77-c162b9fc5de2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616740} {:answer/id #uuid "dbcdff5c-fc94-5c25-ad88-bd265bf3a798" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616768}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "11608109-63f4-5381-863e-6e92792cc660" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616410} :answer-field/id #uuid "a65d4c6c-16b6-5e9e-beb1-c18412078827" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616898}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "2dc2fed3-d655-5205-951d-af8d7bb52e4b" :question/math-academy-id "q-142473" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix and  $det(A)=0?$ \n\nI. $A$ is invertible\n\nII. $\\text{Col}(A)\\ne {R}^{4}$\n\nIII. $\\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\}$" :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $$\n\\displaystyle \\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{4} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col)}(A)=4=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null)}(A)=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn. \n\n- Statement I is false. A matrix $A$ is invertible if and only if $det(A)\\ne 0.$ Since here we have $det(A)=0,$ our matrix $A$ is not invertible.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, since $A$ is *not* invertible, we must have $\\text{Col}(A)\\ne {R}^{4}.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $A$ is not invertible,  it must be $\\text{Null}(A)\\ne \\{0\\}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186617001 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ffa830c-d80c-50f1-a9d5-fe1ebcd7331a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616472} {:answer/id #uuid "74e42cb9-e4af-5881-b608-c6f11cb10b48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "n" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616580} {:answer/id #uuid "a7630b66-b242-57a5-9ee0-cb303aa7fd5d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{0\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616679} {:answer/id #uuid "b0012022-5d79-54b1-9714-0e41233affc9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}^{n}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616695} {:answer/id #uuid "ffae7155-96c2-535c-bde8-3a20e9b83925" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616821}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b0012022-5d79-54b1-9714-0e41233affc9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}^{n}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616695} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a148ab1-c122-59b6-a4a9-dfb8bdba9c0c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616871}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "9c53dbaf-3ce4-5d86-a287-de9fed2a2135" :question/math-academy-id "q-141193" :question/problem "$$\nA\\text{ is invertible}\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)=\\bbox[3pt,white,border:2px solid Gainsboro]{\\phantom{W}} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=n=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the equivalence above, where $A$ is an $n\\,\\times \\,n$ matrix. Which of the following should be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the *invertible matrix theorem* states the following: \n\n*Let $A$ be an $n\\,\\times \\,n$ matrix. Then we have the following equivalence:*\n\n$$\nA\\text{ is invertible}\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=n=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expression is ${R}^{n}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186617003 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04c50643-01aa-57fa-8703-551f411bcef7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616382} {:answer/id #uuid "341e787a-6216-56d1-addd-83742093725f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616459} {:answer/id #uuid "bc33d81e-9442-5b3d-9e29-5ebf4f6366a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616713} {:answer/id #uuid "d5396c66-36ca-5609-9c8e-2f99af1e2e6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616758} {:answer/id #uuid "e3317a2c-6551-5c55-9f93-e3277b68058b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616775}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e3317a2c-6551-5c55-9f93-e3277b68058b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616775} :answer-field/id #uuid "48d03ec9-bb33-5a1b-9a2d-866361f6881e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616852}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "a20e0f6e-9a4b-59f0-b28f-3a10b5209120" :question/math-academy-id "q-141205" :question/problem "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $det(A)\\ne 0,$ then $\\text{__________}\\,.$*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\nI. $A$ is invertible\n\nII. All columns of $A$ are pivot columns\n\nIII. $Ax=0$ has no non-trivial solution" :question/worked-solution "The invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $$\n\\displaystyle \\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=n=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $det(A)\\ne 0,$ then $A$ is invertible.* $\\,✓$\n\nSince $det(A)\\ne 0,$ the matrix $A$ must be invertible.\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $det(A)\\ne 0,$ then all columns of $A$ are pivot columns.* $\\,✓$ \n\nIndeed, since $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{dim(Col}(A))=n,$ which means that all columns of $A$ are pivot columns.\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $det(A)\\ne 0,$ then $Ax=0$ has no non-trivial solution.* $\\,✓$\n\nIndeed, since $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\},$ which means that $Ax=0$ has no non-trivial solution.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186617034 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02717221-4f50-5e06-99ab-b59d6c370818" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616376} {:answer/id #uuid "4362c2da-1b14-5a05-82ec-cd9d02715c27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616481} {:answer/id #uuid "a7e5b857-ddf6-57fa-9bba-e751dd4041cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616681} {:answer/id #uuid "c3aeddf3-6a3f-5940-a84a-a0d812268bed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616728} {:answer/id #uuid "e7ca4f0f-0cea-584c-9154-5654b6b76388" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616781}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a7e5b857-ddf6-57fa-9bba-e751dd4041cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616681} :answer-field/id #uuid "2903c293-1eda-5011-b735-91c9fbb84274" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616841}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "f35a0916-c2f9-5592-8918-2772549e2c23" :question/math-academy-id "q-141197" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix and  $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{5}?$ \n\nI. $A$ is invertible\n\nII. $\\text{rank}(A)=6$\n\nIII. $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0$" :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $$\n\\displaystyle \\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{5} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=5=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn. \n\n- Statement I is true. By the invertible matrix theorem,  $A$ is invertible because $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{5}.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since,\n\n$$\n\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{5}\\,⟹\\,\\text{rank}(A)=\\text{dim(Col}(A))=5.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $A$ is invertible,  it must be $\\text{dim(Null}(A))=0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186627687 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "217d00e3-6085-5217-9e0f-bc0ed267a659" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186627152} {:answer/id #uuid "4d216911-9fdd-5d94-9372-99c99ec03e85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186627226} {:answer/id #uuid "c69e47ba-4ae4-5ccc-94e3-da31c8bee3bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186627431} {:answer/id #uuid "cb083657-c6c3-5e24-8fd7-4d2f8e37c426" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186627440} {:answer/id #uuid "d61c0f82-de33-5eb0-80d0-e768ca91585e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186627460}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cb083657-c6c3-5e24-8fd7-4d2f8e37c426" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186627440} :answer-field/id #uuid "5be541ef-8f3c-5ccd-a814-640b71ca741c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186627583}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "48e66ecf-d81b-50c1-a8a1-a9e2ad76a682" :question/math-academy-id "q-141217" :question/problem "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{Col}(A)⊂{R}^{n},$ then $\\text{__________}\\,.$*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\nI. $\\text{nullity}(A)=0$\n\nII. $\\text{Null}(A)\\ne \\{0\\}$\n\nIII. $det(A)=0$" :question/worked-solution "The invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $$\n\\displaystyle \\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=n=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{Col}(A)⊂{R}^{n},$ then  $\\text{nullity}(A)=0.$* $\\,\\times$\n\nBy the invertible matrix theorem, if  $\\text{Col}(A)$ is not ${R}^{n}$ then  $A$ is not an invertible matrix and  so we must have $\\text{nullity}(A)\\ne 0.$\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{Col}(A)⊂{R}^{n},$ then  $\\text{Null}(A)\\ne \\{0\\}.$* $\\,✓$\n\nIndeed, by the invertible matrix theorem, if  $\\text{Col}(A)$ is not ${R}^{n}$ then  $A$ is not an invertible matrix and  so we must have $\\text{Null}(A)\\ne \\{0\\}.$\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{Col}(A)⊂{R}^{n},$ then  $det(A)=0.$* $\\,✓$  \n\nSince $\\text{Col}(A)⊂{R}^{n},$ then according to the invertible matrix theorem, $A$ is not invertible, which means $det(A)=0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186627692 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00e0fc9f-7385-5c7b-ae3b-103b9330e3c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186627091} {:answer/id #uuid "1c378646-9302-5a64-9728-c1b51529df79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186627145} {:answer/id #uuid "708def97-75ed-58ef-a2bf-6861c83ab912" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186627282} {:answer/id #uuid "9b8fd432-6f8f-51c7-bfbb-559a7ea21b24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186627354} {:answer/id #uuid "a6c36613-e9d3-5ba7-91ca-a44714c54624" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186627371}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "00e0fc9f-7385-5c7b-ae3b-103b9330e3c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186627091} :answer-field/id #uuid "48b9389d-612d-5d40-ba4a-42e4e4c73b9b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186627573}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "624ebabe-0dfa-5173-b265-5c678170209c" :question/math-academy-id "q-142478" :question/problem "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ invertible matrix,  then $\\text{__________}$ .*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\nI. $\\text{Null}(A)\\ne \\{0\\}$\n\nII. $\\text{rank}(A)=3$\n\nIII. $Ax=0$ has only the trivial solution" :question/worked-solution "If $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $$\n\\displaystyle \\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{3} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=3=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ invertible matrix,  then  $\\text{Null}(A)\\ne \\{0\\}.$* $\\,\\times$ \n\nSince $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem,  we have $\\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\}.$\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ invertible matrix,  then $\\text{rank}(A)=3.$* $\\,✓$\n\nIndeed, since $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem,  we have $\\text{dim(Col}(A))=3=\\text{rank}(A).$\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ invertible matrix,  then $Ax=0$ has only the trivial solution.* $\\,✓$ \n\nIndeed, since $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\},$ which means that $Ax=0$ has only the trivial solution.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186627715 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2db7a114-79ca-5bba-8124-a7181493b13b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{rank}(A)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186627175} {:answer/id #uuid "3d068235-7187-58b5-8e9a-5227645c538c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{Col}(A)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186627198} {:answer/id #uuid "5962a640-dcc7-5027-bb07-b17fe801639b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.t