 #uuid "7849c7a6-8771-5340-9ff8-55577a1a84b5" :question/math-academy-id "q-141347" :question/problem "$$\nA\\text{ is invertible}\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=n=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=\\bbox[3pt,white,border:2px solid Gainsboro]{\\phantom{W}}=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the equivalence above, where $A$ is an $n\\,\\times \\,n$ matrix. Which of the following should be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the *invertible matrix theorem* states the following: \n\n*Let $A$ be an $n\\,\\times \\,n$ matrix. Then we have the following equivalence:*\n\n$$\nA\\text{ is invertible}\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=n=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expression is $0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186662343 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1bb0df87-6b66-5944-b1dd-454ba552f9db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186661659} {:answer/id #uuid "228b7b0a-3160-5b2a-b1d1-61d079480a0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186661678} {:answer/id #uuid "314661e8-5e45-5943-b8e5-9fcd7ab80791" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186661704} {:answer/id #uuid "34d03e7e-d18b-5ca3-92b3-37a181e42b4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186661714} {:answer/id #uuid "4c9f293d-624e-5ed9-913e-8cb4be3d342c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186661762}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1bb0df87-6b66-5944-b1dd-454ba552f9db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186661659} :answer-field/id #uuid "f75f7499-83c9-59af-ba8f-207dccb35553" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186662249}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "dae4fbb5-bcbf-541b-9afd-ea52e3dddf91" :question/math-academy-id "q-47604" :question/problem "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{Col}(A)⊂{R}^{n},$ then $\\text{__________}\\,.$*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\nI. $\\text{rank}(A)=n$\n\nII. $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0$\n\nIII. $A$ has $n$ pivot columns" :question/worked-solution "The invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $$\n\\displaystyle \\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=n=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{Col}(A)⊂{R}^{n},$ then  $\\text{rank}(A)=n.$* $\\,\\times$\n\nSince $\\text{Col}(A)⊂{R}^{n},$ then we have $\\text{rank}(A)=\\text{dim(Col}(A))\\le n-1\\ne n.$\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{Col}(A)⊂{R}^{n},$ then  $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0.$* $\\,✓$\n\nIndeed, by the invertible matrix theorem, if  $\\text{Col}(A)$ is not ${R}^{n}$ then  $A$ is not an invertible matrix and  so we must have $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0.$\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{Col}(A)⊂{R}^{n},$ then  $A$ has $n$ pivot columns.* $\\,\\times$  \n\nSince $\\text{Col}(A)⊂{R}^{n},$ the matrix $A$ can have at most  $n-1$ pivot columns.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186662344 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "410d25ee-90ba-563c-943d-db4052119c78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186661739} {:answer/id #uuid "946260af-9902-5d47-9925-fbe161873cf3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186661880} {:answer/id #uuid "9d18bcd5-71b2-5b84-bee1-7f8b1aefb062" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186661898} {:answer/id #uuid "c6f069db-9ecb-576b-a1d9-18ecf527a428" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186661962} {:answer/id #uuid "cb788b15-b090-5bb3-9a67-25e175ed8608" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186661974}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c6f069db-9ecb-576b-a1d9-18ecf527a428" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186661962} :answer-field/id #uuid "f1fe6272-f996-503c-bc14-a61bb015472a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186662247}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "db5a5ae3-0add-50b7-955f-ff73e4e003cc" :question/math-academy-id "q-141214" :question/problem "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $det(A)=0,$ then $\\text{__________}\\,.$*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\nI. $\\text{Null}(A)$ has no basis\n\nII. $\\text{Col}(A)\\ne {R}^{n}$\n\nIII. $\\text{dim(Null}(A))=0$" :question/worked-solution "The invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $$\n\\displaystyle \\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=n=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $det(A)=0,$ then $\\text{Null}(A)$ has no basis.* $\\,\\times$  \n\nSince $det(A)=0,$ it must be $Ax=0$ has non-trivial solution, which means $\\text{Null}(A)$ has basis.\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $det(A)=0,$ then $\\text{Col}(A)\\ne {R}^{n}.$*$\\,✓$\n\nIndeed, $A$ is not invertible because $det(A)=0.$  Since $A$ is not invertible, according to the invertible matrix theorem, it must be $\\text{Col}(A)\\ne {R}^{n}.$\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $det(A)=0,$ then $\\text{dim(Null}(A))=0.$*  $\\,\\times$\n\nSince $det(A)=0,$ then $Ax=0$ has non-trivial solution, which means that $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186673117 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15b93aa7-c591-5841-aa3a-357d8bf16eef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673116} {:answer/id #uuid "45cde434-4d75-5c09-9b0f-35b920274076" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673121} {:answer/id #uuid "52405711-96a4-58b9-b20b-772647cc4c5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673122} {:answer/id #uuid "70a7bdca-b802-5569-bfd3-d23438559962" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673127} {:answer/id #uuid "cddf6d9c-c0bf-57b1-b126-0839ec3bed59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673144}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "15b93aa7-c591-5841-aa3a-357d8bf16eef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673116} :answer-field/id #uuid "e61f64c2-6321-5d18-9115-5e8492b4d1ce" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673145}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "24f7a599-64fa-59b0-bc94-5119ac1b11b5" :question/problem "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\operatorname{Null}(A)=\\{0\\}$, then $\\underline{\\phantom{xxxxxx}}$.*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\nI. $\\operatorname{Null}(A)$ has no basis\n\nII. $\\operatorname{Col}(A)\\subsetneq\\mathbb{R}^{n}$\n\nIII. $\\operatorname{nullity}(A)=0$" :question/worked-solution "The invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}A\\text{ is invertible}\\\\\\Updownarrow\\\\\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{Col}(A)&=\\mathbb{R}^{n}\\\\\\dim(\\operatorname{Col}(A))&=n=\\operatorname{rank}(A)\\\\\\operatorname{Null}(A)&=\\{0\\}\\\\\\dim(\\operatorname{Null}(A))&=0=\\operatorname{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\operatorname{Null}(A)=\\{0\\}$, then $\\operatorname{Null}(A)$ has no basis.* ×\n\nEvery finite-dimensional subspace has a basis. The zero subspace has the empty basis.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\operatorname{Null}(A)=\\{0\\}$, then $\\operatorname{Col}(A)\\subsetneq\\mathbb{R}^{n}$.* ×\n\nThe given condition implies $\\operatorname{rank}(A)=n$ and $\\operatorname{nullity}(A)=0$. Thus $\\operatorname{Col}(A)=\\mathbb{R}^{n}$.\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\operatorname{Null}(A)=\\{0\\}$, then $\\operatorname{nullity}(A)=0$.* ✓\n\nThe given condition implies $\\operatorname{rank}(A)=n$ and $\\operatorname{nullity}(A)=0$. Thus $\\operatorname{nullity}(A)=0$.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is III only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186673124 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09e0c05b-14aa-5e14-b955-527ebc07ec4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673113} {:answer/id #uuid "3b0d39f6-4254-5d22-bf4e-6febe4ad2533" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673119}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3b0d39f6-4254-5d22-bf4e-6febe4ad2533" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673119} :answer-field/id #uuid "956051b9-5768-5547-88b9-3b7e942076a5" :answer-field/key "$\\det(A)=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673134} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "348adaf6-7787-565e-9ff4-1f701aa97384" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673118} {:answer/id #uuid "eb5e628e-f4dc-5d13-9581-7e8bb52ecd66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673147}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "348adaf6-7787-565e-9ff4-1f701aa97384" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673118} :answer-field/id #uuid "987163a9-96d8-5ed7-b484-24cd137c96e9" :answer-field/key "$\\operatorname{Col}(A)=\\mathbb{R}^{7}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673137} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14c0ef31-2044-5855-a7a9-cab2011298ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673115} {:answer/id #uuid "a0a583d1-5c19-57bb-b0b1-2de813730ab5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673140}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "14c0ef31-2044-5855-a7a9-cab2011298ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673115} :answer-field/id #uuid "b0d31553-b93e-5bf7-a7e6-04e42a08a1de" :answer-field/key "$A$ has fewer than $7$ pivot columns" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673143}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "635f4b7d-7d59-52ae-8c0d-6343e80d6951" :question/problem "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $7\\times 7$ matrix and $\\operatorname{nullity}(A)=0$, then $\\underline{\\phantom{xxxxxx}}$.*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}A\\text{ is invertible}\\\\\\Updownarrow\\\\\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{Col}(A)&=\\mathbb{R}^{7}\\\\\\dim(\\operatorname{Col}(A))&=7=\\operatorname{rank}(A)\\\\\\operatorname{Null}(A)&=\\{0\\}\\\\\\dim(\\operatorname{Null}(A))&=0=\\operatorname{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $7\\times 7$ matrix and $\\operatorname{nullity}(A)=0$, then $\\det(A)=0$.* ×\n\nThe given condition implies $\\operatorname{rank}(A)=7$ and $\\operatorname{nullity}(A)=0$. Thus $\\det(A)\\ne 0$.\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $7\\times 7$ matrix and $\\operatorname{nullity}(A)=0$, then $\\operatorname{Col}(A)=\\mathbb{R}^{7}$.* ✓\n\nThe given condition implies $\\operatorname{rank}(A)=7$ and $\\operatorname{nullity}(A)=0$. Thus $\\operatorname{Col}(A)=\\mathbb{R}^{7}$.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $7\\times 7$ matrix and $\\operatorname{nullity}(A)=0$, then $A$ has fewer than $7$ pivot columns.* ×\n\nThe given condition implies $\\operatorname{rank}(A)=7$ and $\\operatorname{nullity}(A)=0$. Thus $A$ has $7$ pivot columns.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\operatorname{Col}(A)=\\mathbb{R}^{7}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186673141 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "81068501-c0e2-5f32-acb0-2aace6ed6c10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673132} {:answer/id #uuid "99a5c457-06a2-52cc-aa45-339994a36685" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673138}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "81068501-c0e2-5f32-acb0-2aace6ed6c10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673132} :answer-field/id #uuid "01abd1c7-c59f-5c99-9277-f9537d6b88ca" :answer-field/key "$A$ has $n$ pivot columns" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673111} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5d553a7c-18de-5cec-850b-80701a20b3ca" :answ