tion "The invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}A\\text{ is invertible}\\\\\\Updownarrow\\\\\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{Col}(A)&=\\mathbb{R}^{n}\\\\\\dim(\\operatorname{Col}(A))&=n=\\operatorname{rank}(A)\\\\\\operatorname{Null}(A)&=\\{0\\}\\\\\\dim(\\operatorname{Null}(A))&=0=\\operatorname{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\operatorname{Col}(A)=\\mathbb{R}^{n}$, then $A$ is **not** invertible.* ×\n\nThe given condition implies $\\operatorname{rank}(A)=n$ and $\\operatorname{nullity}(A)=0$. Thus $A$ is invertible.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\operatorname{Col}(A)=\\mathbb{R}^{n}$, then $\\operatorname{rank}(A)<n$.* ×\n\nThe given condition implies $\\operatorname{rank}(A)=n$ and $\\operatorname{nullity}(A)=0$. Thus $\\operatorname{rank}(A)=n$.\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\operatorname{Col}(A)=\\mathbb{R}^{n}$, then $A$ has $n$ pivot columns.* ✓\n\nThe given condition implies $\\operatorname{rank}(A)=n$ and $\\operatorname{nullity}(A)=0$. Thus $A$ has $n$ pivot columns.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $A$ has $n$ pivot columns."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186673148 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "040ad0ff-3100-5425-b2f1-da7e669a2b4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673112} {:answer/id #uuid "4238513f-e322-530e-9565-e1ef6525b9d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673120} {:answer/id #uuid "756e0384-4d12-5af5-b55c-3d54c0e1e087" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673130}