not** invertible.\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\operatorname{Null}(A)\\ne\\{0\\}$, then $\\det(A)=0$.* ✓\n\nThe given condition implies $\\operatorname{rank}(A)<n$ and $\\operatorname{nullity}(A)>0$. Thus $\\det(A)=0$.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\operatorname{Null}(A)\\ne\\{0\\}$, then $\\operatorname{rank}(A)=n$.* ×\n\nThe given condition implies $\\operatorname{rank}(A)<n$ and $\\operatorname{nullity}(A)>0$. Thus $\\operatorname{rank}(A)<n$.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is I and II only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186673150 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6cf403e2-fc73-51e8-93ac-21bd4fa4deb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673126} {:answer/id #uuid "735ac19d-aa52-5baf-a48d-1b36bd66de03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673128} {:answer/id #uuid "7aa16602-e7c9-54cd-a27f-713bd6b96dc4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673131} {:answer/id #uuid "9b066337-30b7-5051-a050-f4cc7caba6b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673139} {:answer/id #uuid "f20ce81b-8827-55b8-8eda-03664eee7b4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673149}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f20ce81b-8827-55b8-8eda-03664eee7b4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673149} :answer-field/id #uuid "e7a0c1cc-ebfa-5947-959b-5472ae9f3909" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673146}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "f57a7c6f-101e-5b33-aef0-c7309a1bc9ae" :question/problem "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\operatorname{Col}(A)=\\mathbb{R}^{n}$, then $\\underline{\\phantom{xxxxxx}}$.*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\nI. $\\operatorname{rank}(A)<n$\n\nII. $\\operatorname{nullity}(A)>0$\n\nIII. $A$ has $n$ pivot columns" :question/worked-solution "The invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}A\\text{ is invertible}\\\\\\Updownarrow\\\\\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{Col}(A)&=\\mathbb{R}^{n}\\\\\\dim(\\operatorname{Col}(A))&=n=\\operatorname{rank}(A)\\\\\\operatorname{Null}(A)&=\\{0\\}\\\\\\dim(\\operatorname{Null}(A))&=0=\\operatorname{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\operatorname{Col}(A)=\\mathbb{R}^{n}$, then $\\operatorname{rank}(A)<n$.* ×\n\nThe given condition implies $\\operatorname{rank}(A)=n$ and $\\operatorname{nullity}(A)=0$. Thus $\\operatorname{rank}(A)=n$.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\operatorname{Col}(A)=\\mathbb{R}^{n}$, then $\\operatorname{nullity}(A)>0$.* ×\n\nThe given condition implies $\\operatorname{rank}(A)=n$ and $\\operatorname{nullity}(A)=0$. Thus $\\operatorname{nullity}(A)=0$.\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\operatorname{Col}(A)=\\mathbb{R}^{n}$, then $A$ has $n$ pivot columns.* ✓\n\nThe given condition implies $\\operatorname{rank}(A)=n$ and $\\operatorname{nullity}(A)=0$. Thus $A$ has $n$ pivot columns.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is III only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186673154 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c4b21a8-5857-5ef8-bfd3-a65eb1a523c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673165} {:answer/id #uuid "9a973bcf-70db-5a89-a689-b55ce1af4a80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\mathbb{R}^{n}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673172} {:answer/id #uuid "b1783284-0306-56fc-9b19-67e44e5dc329" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{0\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673175} {:answer/id #uuid "b2583ecf-8bbb-5a3a-9b7b-8101ae883bee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "n" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673176} {:answer/id #uuid "fbee72da-3edd-5510-88b6-7c2b8327142e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "n+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673187}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9a973bcf-70db-5a89-a689-b55ce1af4a80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\mathbb{R}^{n}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673172} :answer-field/id #uuid "37c4b2c7-8383-560f-9c33-c4c490b999a7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673159}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "1032f2f7-ec7b-5de6-aa13-e05a715721ed" :question/problem "$$\n\\begin{gathered}A\\text{ is }\\text{invertible} \\\\ \\Updownarrow \\\\ \\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{Col}(A) &=\\underline{\\phantom{WWWW}} \\\\ \\dim(\\operatorname{Col}(A)) &=n=\\operatorname{rank}(A) \\\\ \\operatorname{Null}(A) &=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\dim(\\operatorname{Null}(A)) &=0=\\operatorname{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\right.\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nConsider the equivalence above, where $A$ is a real $n\\times n$ matrix and $n$ is a positive integer. Which of the following should be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the *invertible matrix theorem* states the following:\n\n*Let $A$ be a real $n\\times n$ matrix. Then we have the following equivalence:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}A\\text{ is }\\text{invertible} \\\\ \\Updownarrow \\\\ \\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{Col}(A) &=\\mathbb{R}^{n} \\\\ \\dim(\\operatorname{Col}(A)) &=n=\\operatorname{rank}(A) \\\\ \\operatorname{Null}(A) &=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\dim(\\operatorname{Null}(A)) &=0=\\operatorname{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\right.\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expression is $\\mathbb{R}^{n}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186673160 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24aefc48-e16c-5618-bdd1-7cd543bb8643" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "n+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673157} {:answer/id #uuid "727f263c-b6ba-55bd-966e-9a9531a0d698" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{Col}(A)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673166} {:answer/id #uuid "8f8bd431-03aa-5ea5-bc71-2f5af4fa9a1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{Null}(A)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673170} {:answer/id #uuid "a0f5740c-26dd-5513-be6b-f8806f637828" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\dim(\\operatorname{Col}(A))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673173} {:answer/id #uuid "c5ba6822-20cf-5269-a265-dbe1fd69f77e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\dim(\\operatorname{Null}(A))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673179}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a0f5740c-26dd-5513-be6b-f8806f637828" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\dim(\\operatorname{Col}(A))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673173} :answer-field/id #uuid "f9311aa1-c302-